{"id":2603,"path":"/grammar-points/a2/asking-questions-in-english/","parentId":542,"order":0,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a2","depth":3,"title":"Asking questions in English: Question forms","seo":{"title":"Asking questions in English: Question forms - Test-English","description":"Learn how to ask questions in English in this A2 Pre-intermediate grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A2Question-forms.png"},"modified":"2026-09-25T22:24:28","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct forms to complete the questions below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"320\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct&nbsp;forms to complete the questions below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"321\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Fill in the gaps with&nbsp;question words.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"323\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 4</h3> <h5>Write questions for the underlined words.</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: We won <span><strong>a trip to Hawaii</strong>.</span> ⇒ <span class=\"textGap\">What did you win</span>?</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"322\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<h2>Word order in questions: Grammar chart</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-10705\" src=\"/media/uploads/Questions-word-order.new_.png\" alt=\"Infographic explaining the word order in English questions, with examples for standard question order and questions using the auxiliary verb 'be'. The chart illustrates the placement of question words, auxiliary verbs, subjects, and main verbs or adjectives for forming questions in English.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4>Questions in general</h4> <p>If we want to ask a question in English, the order is <strong>QWASM</strong>: <strong>Question word, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/auxiliary-verbs-do-be-and-have/\"><strong>Auxiliary verb</strong></a>, Subject, Main verb</strong>. In <strong>Yes-No questions</strong> (questions where the answer is <strong>yes</strong> or <strong>no</strong>), there is no Question Word.</p> <h4>Questions with&nbsp;<strong>be</strong> as the main verb</h4> <p>When&nbsp;<a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple-forms-of-to-be/\"><strong>be</strong></a> is the main verb, it is used as the&nbsp;<strong>Auxiliary</strong> in the question, and then we don’t have a <strong>Main verb</strong> after the Subject.</p> <h4>Auxiliary verbs</h4> <p>In the position of <strong>Auxiliary</strong>, we can use <strong>be</strong>, <strong>do</strong>, <strong>have</strong> or any modal verb: <strong><a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/can-cant/\"><strong>can</strong></a>, could, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/will-and-shall/\"><strong>will</strong></a>, would, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/should-shouldnt/\"><strong>should</strong></a></strong>, etc.<br> <br> <strong>Have</strong> is only an auxiliary verb in the form&nbsp;<a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/have-got/\"><strong>have got</strong></a> and in the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/present-perfect/\"><strong>present perfect</strong></a>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Have</strong></span> you <span><strong>got</strong></span> any brothers or sisters? </em></li> <li><em>What <strong><span>have</span></strong> you <span><strong>cooked</strong></span> for lunch? </em></li> </ul> <p>For other uses of <strong>have</strong>, we need an auxiliary verb (<strong>do</strong>, <strong>did</strong>) for questions.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>What time <span><strong>had you</strong></span> dinner yesterday? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>What time <span><strong>did you have</strong></span> dinner yesterday? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Have you</strong></span> to do it now? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Do you</strong></span>&nbsp;<span><strong>have</strong></span> to do it now? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <p><strong>Have got</strong> only has a present form. It does not have a past form.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Had you got</strong></span> many toys when you were a child? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Did you</strong></span>&nbsp;<span><strong>have</strong></span> many toys when you were a child? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h2>Question words</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-10709\" src=\"/media/uploads/Question-words.new_.png\" alt=\"Colorful educational chart of question words in English, categorized by their use such as 'WHO' for person, 'WHERE' for place, and 'HOW OLD' for age, with example dialogues for each word\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4><strong>How much</strong></h4> <p>We can use <strong>how much</strong> to ask about the price of something.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><em><span><strong>How much</strong></span> is the jacket?</em></em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>How</strong> + adjective</h4> <p>We can use <strong>how + adjective</strong> (any adjective) as a question word.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>How tall</strong></span> are you?</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>How fast</strong></span> is your car?</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>Which</strong> vs <strong>what</strong></h4> <p>We can use <strong>which + noun</strong>, and we can also use <strong>what + noun</strong>. We use <strong>which</strong> when there are a small number of possible answers.&nbsp;Look at the difference:</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Which</strong></span> car do you like, the red or the blue?&nbsp;</em>(there is a small number of possible answers)</li> <li><em>‘<span><strong>What</strong></span> car have you got?’ ‘A Mercedes.’</em> (many possible answers)</li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":320,"questions":[{"id":2763,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>How often <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to the dentist?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["you do go","do you go","you go"]}]},{"id":2764,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>How many brothers and sisters <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["you have","have you got","have you"]}]},{"id":2765,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What time <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> pick me up?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["you can","can you","do you can"]}]},{"id":2766,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Where <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> last night?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["did Tim be","Tim was","was Tim"]}]},{"id":2767,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> John this morning?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Did you see","You saw","You did see"]}]},{"id":2768,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Why <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> that box there?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["put you","you did put","did you put"]}]},{"id":2769,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> with the scissors?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["are you doing","you are doing","do you are doing"]}]},{"id":2770,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>When <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a decision?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["she will make","will she make","make she"]}]},{"id":2771,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What time <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you tomorrow?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["should I call","do I should call","I should call"]}]},{"id":2772,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Who <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to the party?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Sandra invited","Sandra did invite","did Sandra invite"]}]}]},{"id":321,"questions":[{"id":2773,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>How long _____ in Paris?</div>","choices":[{"id":4814,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>did you stay</span>"},{"id":4815,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>were you stay</span>"},{"id":4816,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>you stayed</span>"}]},{"id":2774,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>How _____ to Barcelona?</div>","choices":[{"id":4817,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>did you travel</span>"},{"id":4818,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>you travelled</span>"},{"id":4819,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>were you travel</span>"}]},{"id":2775,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Which _____ ?</div>","choices":[{"id":4820,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>your favourite colour is</span>"},{"id":4821,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>does your favourite colour be</span>"},{"id":4822,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>is your favourite colour</span>"}]},{"id":2776,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>What instrument _____ when you were a child?</div>","choices":[{"id":4823,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>could play you</span>"},{"id":4824,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>could you play</span>"},{"id":4825,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>you could play</span>"}]},{"id":2777,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Why _____ there?</div>","choices":[{"id":4826,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>that man's standing</span>"},{"id":4827,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>does that man is standing</span>"},{"id":4828,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>is that man standing</span>"}]},{"id":2778,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>How much _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":4829,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>she has lost</span>"},{"id":4830,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>does she have lost</span>"},{"id":4831,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>has she lost</span>"}]},{"id":2779,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>What time _____ to arrive?</div>","choices":[{"id":4832,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>is she going </span>"},{"id":4833,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>she's going </span>"},{"id":4834,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>is going</span>"}]},{"id":2780,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Where _____ last summer?</div>","choices":[{"id":4835,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>went he</span>"},{"id":4836,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>did he go</span>"},{"id":4837,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>he went</span>"}]},{"id":2781,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>What time _____ to bed?</div>","choices":[{"id":4838,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>children should</span>"},{"id":4839,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>should children go</span>"},{"id":4840,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>do children should go</span>"}]},{"id":2782,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>When _____ me?</div>","choices":[{"id":4841,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>can you see</span>"},{"id":4842,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>can see</span>"},{"id":4843,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>you can see</span>"}]}]},{"id":323,"questions":[{"id":2793,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span class=\"tabtext\">A: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> do you live?</span><br><span class=\"tab\">B: In a small town near here.</span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2794,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span class=\"tabtext\">A: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> was at the party?</span><br><span class=\"tab\">B: Frederick, Leslie, and some other friends.</span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2795,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span class=\"tabtext\">A: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> did you say to Laura?</span><br><span class=\"tab\">B: Nothing.</span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2796,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> box do you prefer, the small one or the big one?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2797,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span class=\"tabtext\">A: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> do you go out?</span><br><span class=\"tab\">B: Every Saturday.</span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2798,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span class=\"tabtext\">A: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> are you going to visit me?</span><br><span class=\"tab\">B: Next Sunday.</span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2799,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span class=\"tabtext\">A: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> didn't you tell me anything?</span><br><span class=\"tab\">B: Because I was afraid.</span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2800,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span class=\"tabtext\">A: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> sugar do you want in your coffee?</span><br><span class=\"tab\">B: Two spoonfuls, please.</span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2801,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span class=\"tabtext\">A: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> shall we meet?</span><br><span class=\"tab\">B: At 7?</span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2802,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span class=\"tabtext\">A: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> is she going to stay?</span><br><span class=\"tab\">B: Just a couple of days.</span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]},{"id":322,"questions":[{"id":2783,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We have to clean the office <strong><span>in the morning</span></strong>. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the office?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2784,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She writes <span><strong>two</strong></span> pages every day. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> every day?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2785,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He'll find a job <span><strong>soon</strong></span>. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a job?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2786,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Yesterday she called me <span><strong>because she needed my help</strong></span>. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> yesterday?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2787,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She&nbsp;has breakfast at home <span><strong>twice a week</strong></span>. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> breakfast at home?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2788,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The fish and chips cost <span><strong>6 pounds</strong></span> on Mondays. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> on Mondays?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2789,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I'm living <span><strong>in a small town</strong></span> now. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> now?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2790,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The cat is <span><strong>under the chair</strong></span>. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2791,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This pen is <span><strong>mine</strong></span>. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2792,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We are going to stay <span><strong>for a couple of weeks</strong></span>. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}